Done. I coded the Hoffman/voting-rights row as BLANK `no-evidence`: HB2492 (2022) is chair-shaped for rung 5 (proof of citizenship at registration), and Hoffman was its prime sponsor and a Yea vote, but the bill was passed and signed in 2022 while he held a different office (State Representative), before his State Senate term began 2023-01-02 — per V5, a record from an earlier office is valid for that office only, so it can't establish the chair for this Senate row. Flagged in `needs_source` that a post-2023 Senate act on this topic is needed.
